WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.240
- Did FTX have sufficient
risk management systems

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.440
and controls to appropriately
monitor any leverage

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.550
the business took on and
the interconnections it had

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.763
with businesses like, again, Alameda?

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.370
- There were virtually
no internal controls

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.320
and no separateness whatsoever.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.320
- So what is the big picture balance loss

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.370
as a result of this bankruptcy?

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.530
How much has FTX lost as a result of this?

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.810
- We don't have exact
numbers, but we know ballpark.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:37.410
Several billion dollars, you
know, in excess of 7 billion.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:38.790
- Can you provide some indication

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.880
of whether customer funds from FTX.com

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.733
were in fact transferred
to Alameda Research?

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.030
- Well, it's definitely assets

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.980
of customers in the .com silo

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.480
were transferred to Alameda,
no question about it.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:58.730
We have not seen this at
this stage from the US silo

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.110
but of course, you know,
we do have one concern

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.000
and that's the concern we're chasing down,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.980
which is whether or
not there's co-mingling

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:09.980
between that .com silo
and the US silo exchanges.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.780
And the reason for that is we know

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.220
that there was sort of
common control and access

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:20.640
of authorized users at this
most senior management level

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.900
amongst all of the assets.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.090
So it's something we have to focus on.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.730
We haven't seen evidence right now of that

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.050
but certainly that's
something that we need

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:29.520
to investigate and trace.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.750
- Are you yet in a position

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.220
to be able to describe,
summarize the assets

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.513
that Alameda had?

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.680
- We do have an inventory
of the investments we made.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:44.280
That's pretty clear.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.250
We've got those in the hands
of our investment bankers

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.520
at Perella and we're trying to
understand those investments.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.680
Ultimately, we'll market
those investments.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.833
You'll see this week that
some of those investments

00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:58.230
will be put up for sale.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:01.470
The crypto assets, a little bit different.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.760
What's on the exchanges?

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.593
We can see.

00:02:03.593 --> 00:02:06.210
There's exchanges, about
two dozen exchanges

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:10.260
across the world where we
know we have crypto assets.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.370
They're in our name.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.330
We're securing those

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.150
and we're moving those into cold storage.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.750
We have, you know, other positions

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.306
in cold wallets and hot wallets.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.770
We've got visibility to that.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:23.970
The question really is

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.163
are there wallets that
we don't know about?

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.590
Certainly that is the potential

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.930
because the way this
company was organized,

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:34.080
there may be wallets that
don't have our names,

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.990
we don't know where they are,
and that's gonna be, you know,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.580
a difficult task ahead of us.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:39.450
But what we can see

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.660
and what we have visibility to,
we're grabbing control over.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:43.493
- What are some

00:02:43.493 --> 00:02:44.730
of the biggest questions you still have

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.430
for Mr. Bankman-Fried
and his associates now

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.680
that you've been through
this for some period?

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.870
- Look, I think the questions we have

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:55.230
are not necessarily
questions for Mr. Fried.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.970
The questions we have are, you know,

00:02:56.970 --> 00:03:00.333
where are the assets, how
do we locate those assets?

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:03.423
It's a mining exercise at this point.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:08.460
And look, at the end of the day,

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.700
we're not gonna be able to
recover all the losses here.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.980
Money was spent that we'll never get back.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.930
There will be losses on
the international side.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:17.673
We're hopeful on the US side.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.600
He'll answer to others
related to what happened here.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.170
Our job is just to, you
know, find the assets

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.210
and try to get customers their money back

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.360
as quickly as possible.

